JPIPHTTPSRequest.swift50–90 checks exposed header text/descriptors before building the extra dictionary, and checks declared body storage using checked arithmetic. Lines93–175 account for the callback Data, retained accumulation capacity, old/new allocation overlap and final exact-sized result copy before further owned allocation/copy. Capacity is represented by allocated Data.count, independently of received bodyCount. Scoped pointer copies use counts/offsets established by checked admission and do not escape or span suspension. URLSession has already allocated callback/header objects before invocation; opaque TLS/network/cache/queued-callback buffers and allocator padding are not claimed as pre-admitted or measured RSS.

